#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Workflow audit (spec #92, ticket #94). Standard library only; run as `python3 -I <path>/audit ...`.
#   audit ledger <event> --worktree <path> ...   append one validated event to the findings ledger (audit ledger --help)
#   audit ledger show --worktree <path>           print every event of the findings ledger, in order; writes nothing
#   audit check --worktree <path>                 print S1-S9, XC and a transcript digest of at most 50 KB; writes no file
#   audit record --worktree <path> --llm <file>   re-run S1-S9 and XC, read L1-L6, write <sha>.json for the pushed tip
#   audit hook pre-tool-use                       deny `gh pr create` without a passing record for the pushed tip
#   audit hook session-start                      register the session (id, transcript path, start time)
# Exit codes of `record`: 0 record written and passed, 1 record written and failed, 2 nothing written.
# Exit codes of `check`: 0 it ran (a failed item is output, not an error), 2 it refused.
# Both hooks must never break a session: a hook error denies a command that matches the gate and changes nothing else.
